@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@ These hold for every record, however it was made.

 ## Money

+- Every batch has its own cost, `costCents` (integer cents per unit; schema
+  3). A batch from a received order costs the order line's `priceCents`;
+  batches that existed before schema 3 took their item's `priceCents` at
+  migration. Stock value is each batch's quantity at its own cost.
 - Money is an integer number of cents. A line (quantity × unit price) is
   rounded to the cent on its own (half up); totals are sums of rounded lines.
   Never sum unrounded amounts.
